  "lexicon_id": "default_v1",
  "source": "default",
  "version": "1",
  "created": "2026-10-12",
  "notes": [
    "Shipped, hand-written, no-key lexicon. SPEC.md 4.3 requires that the pipeline never",
    "depends on the induction stage existing, so this file is the fallback for every run.",
    "It is deliberately small and finance-specific: the general-purpose core is VADER,",
    "which ships its own lexicon and is used by sentiment.method=vader_plus_lexicon.",
    "polarity is signed and in [-1,1]; weight is a confidence in [0,1] and multiplies it.",
    "family=polarity: general signed sentiment word.",
    "family=bullish/bearish: finance directional vocabulary (the 'finance list').",
    "family=uncertainty: hedging language, scored as a share, not as polarity.",
    "family=attribution: reported speech ('analysts said'), scored as a share.",
    "family=sarcasm: markers whose share is reported as a caveat metric."
  ],
  "negation_patterns": [
    "not", "no", "never", "none", "cannot", "can't", "cant", "won't", "wont", "isn't",
    "isnt", "aren't", "arent", "don't", "dont", "doesn't", "doesnt", "didn't", "didnt",
    "without", "hardly", "barely", "rarely", "n't", "nor", "neither"
  ],
